    "https://www.trentu.ca/humanresources/employment-opportunities/non-academic-positions/important-information-applying": {
      "title": "Important Information Before Applying",
      "description": "Important Information Before Applying - Human Resources - Trent University MyTrent Peterborough Durham GTA Campus Locations Peterborough Durham GTA Online Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Trent Online Summer Courses Continuing Education Study Abroad Academic Calendar Academic Timetable Academic Skills Centre Academic Advising Library Centre for Teaching and Learning Admissions Undergraduate Thinking of Applying Already Applied Received an Offer Accepted My Offer Graduate International Indigenous Returning to Trent Transfer Services & Support Academic Advising Academic Skills Centre Administrative Departments Alumni Services Athletics Campus Security Careerspace Colleges Communications Conferences Financial Aid Financial Services Health & Wellness Indigenous Services Information Technology International Students Learning Support Parking Printshop Recruitment Registrar's Office Residence & Housing Student Clubs TrentU Card Research Research at Trent Research Centres Find an Expert Resources Give to Trent About Trent About Trent Careers Giving to Trent Governance How to Find Us Media News & Events President's Office Staff Directory Trent Facts Contact Us Future Students Undergraduate Thinking of Applying Already Applied Received an Offer Accepted My Offer Graduate International Indigenous Returning to Trent Transfer Current Students The Colleges of Trent Alumni Indigenous Resources and Initiatives Apply Visit Give Peterborough Durham GTA Map Careers Directions Library Site Map Bookstore Skip to main content Peterborough Durham GTA Online MyTrent MENU Human Resources Welcome Employment Opportunities Why Work at Trent Human Resources Services Policies & Forms VIP Contact Trentu.ca Human Resources Employment Opportunities Non-Academic Positions Important Information Before Applying Important Information Before Applying Important Information: While the University appreciates all applications, please note that only candidates selected for an interview will be contacted. In the case of regular/recurring OPSEU positions, the University will consider internal OPSEU applicants first, in accordance with the OPSEU Collective Agreement. A cover letter and resume must be submitted for each position being applied to. Click here to determine if you are required to submit an employment application form. Resumes are accepted for posted positions only, as we do not keep a resume bank. Applications must be received by the application deadline. No late applications will be considered. Internal Applicants: Internal applicants are defined as employees currently holding a regular/recurring OPSEU position. Please clearly indicate on your cover letter that you currently hold a regular or recurring OPSEU position at the University. As per the OPSEU Collective Agreement, Internal applications must be submitted in writing or electronically to Human Resources prior to the deadline. The Department of Human Resources will notify internal applicants that did not meet the posted requirements. External Applicants: External applicants are defined as all individuals not holding a regular or recurring OPSEU position. Contract, Temporary Casual employees and Limited Term Appointments (LTA) are considered external (unless they also hold a regular or recurring OPSEU position). Employees in other bargaining unit groups are considered external when applying for an OPSEU position. The Department of Human Resources will only notify external candidates who successfully secure an interview. Action Menu 50/50 Employee Raffle Draw Anonymous HR Feedback Submission Heart of Trent Awards Non-Academic Positions Non-Academic Positions Important Information Before Applying Frequently Asked Questions Full-Time Faculty Positions (TUFA) Part-Time Faculty Positions (CUPE) Students & Alumni Student Academic Support Positions Related Links VIP - For Employees & Managers Health and Safety Human Rights, Equity & Accessibility Heart of Trent Event Trent University respectfully acknowledges it is located on the treaty and traditional territory of the Mississauga Anishnaabeg. We offer our gratitude to First Peoples for their care for, and teachings about, our earth and our relations. May we honour those teachings. The Campaign For Momentous Action Research Leadership Debate Performance Connection Discovery Ideas Places Stewardship Support Possiblity Peterborough 1600 West Bank Drive Peterborough, ON Canada, K9L 0G2 Toll Free: 1-855-MY-TRENT Find Us Durham Greater Toronto Area 55 Thornton Road South Oshawa, ON Canada, L1J 5Y1 Phone: 905-435-5100 Find Us Social Media Directory Contact Directions Site Map Accessibility Privacy @ Copyright 2026 Trent University This Site Uses Cookies To Enhance Your User Experience View Trent's privacy policy for more information. Accept"
    },
    "https://www.trentu.ca/humanresources/employment-opportunities/non-academic-positions/frequently-asked-questions": {
      "title": "Frequently Asked Questions",
      "description": "Frequently Asked Questions - Human Resources - Trent University MyTrent Peterborough Durham GTA Campus Locations Peterborough Durham GTA Online Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Trent Online Summer Courses Continuing Education Study Abroad Academic Calendar Academic Timetable Academic Skills Centre Academic Advising Library Centre for Teaching and Learning Admissions Undergraduate Thinking of Applying Already Applied Received an Offer Accepted My Offer Graduate International Indigenous Returning to Trent Transfer Services & Support Academic Advising Academic Skills Centre Administrative Departments Alumni Services Athletics Campus Security Careerspace Colleges Communications Conferences Financial Aid Financial Services Health & Wellness Indigenous Services Information Technology International Students Learning Support Parking Printshop Recruitment Registrar's Office Residence & Housing Student Clubs TrentU Card Research Research at Trent Research Centres Find an Expert Resources Give to Trent About Trent About Trent Careers Giving to Trent Governance How to Find Us Media News & Events President's Office Staff Directory Trent Facts Contact Us Future Students Undergraduate Thinking of Applying Already Applied Received an Offer Accepted My Offer Graduate International Indigenous Returning to Trent Transfer Current Students The Colleges of Trent Alumni Indigenous Resources and Initiatives Apply Visit Give Peterborough Durham GTA Map Careers Directions Library Site Map Bookstore Skip to main content Peterborough Durham GTA Online MyTrent MENU Human Resources Welcome Employment Opportunities Why Work at Trent Human Resources Services Policies & Forms VIP Contact Trentu.ca Human Resources Employment Opportunities Non-Academic Positions Frequently Asked Questions Frequently Asked Questions Cannot find the answer to your question below? Please send your question to humanresources@trentu.ca . I am an external candidate, can I still apply to an OPSEU regular/recurring position? How do I know if a job competition is still open and accepting applications? Can I apply for a job, even though the closing date has passed? Will you accept a general resume? How do I apply to student positions? How do I apply to teaching/academic positions? Can I send my resume directly to the hiring manager/department? Who should I address my cover letter to? Can you give me an overview of the hiring process for non-academic positions? Can I call or email the Human Resources Department to see if a position has been filled, and/or check on the status of my application? I've already sent my resume to Trent, will you use it or refer to it for future competitions? Will applications submitted through the External Recruitment Site be reviewed at the same time as applications submitted through the Internal Job Board? Where can I find additional information on the Exempt & OPSEU Recruitment process? I am an external candidate, can I still apply to regular or recurring OPSEU positions? In the case of regular/recurring OPSEU positions, the University will consider internal OPSEU applicants first, in accordance with the OPSEU Collective Agreement . However, external applicants are encouraged to apply to any current job posting. How do I know if a job competition is still open and accepting applications? Any jobs posted are open and accepting applications. If a job is not on our site then it is not an active job competition. Please note, some external advertising sites do not always remove the advertisement once the application deadline has passed. Can I apply for a job, even though the closing date has passed? Late applications will not be considered. Will you accept a general resume? General resumes will not be accepted. How do I apply to student positions? Please visit our Student Academic Support opportunities, or visit Career Space for non-academic student employment opportunities. How do I apply to teaching/academic positions? Please visit the Dean's Office for information on teaching/academic positions . Can I send my resume directly to the hiring manager/department? Applications for Non-Academic (OPSEU & Exempt) positions must be submitted through the External Recruitment Site (external applicants) or the Internal Job Board in VIP (employees and individuals with VIP access), and cannot be sent directly to the hiring manager. All other applications must be submitted via the method specified on the job posting by the posted deadline. Who should I address my cover letter to? Applications are reviewed by an interview committee and therefore do not need to be addressed to a specific person. Can you give me an overview of the hiring process for non-academic positions? The following are generalized and brief steps of the hiring process. Some positions may differ from these steps and the timelines for hiring vary with each position: Job postings are posted on our website anywhere from five working days to \"until filled.\" Once the job posting has closed applications are released to the interview committee for review. The interview committee identifies their short-list. Short-listed candidates are contacted and scheduled for interviews and testing (where applicable). References are checked for the top candidate. A hiring recommendation is forwarded to Human Resources for approval. A verbal offer of employment is extended to the successful candidate. The successful candidate receives a letter confirming their appointment. The remaining short-listed candidates are notified of the committee's decision. Can I call or email the Human Resources Department to see if a position has been filled, and/or check on the status of my application? We appreciate your interest in working at Trent University, however the Department of Human Resources does not provide any information about the status of a job competition to ensure the process is fair for applicants. If the interview committee is interested in your application, you will be contacted. I've already sent my resume to Trent, will you use it or refer to it for future competitions? Due to the volume we receive, we are not able to review prior resume submissions for any future competitions. You must submit an up-to-date covering letter and resume for each individual posting you are interested in. Will applications submitted through the External Recruitment Site be reviewed at the same time as applications submitted through the Internal Job Board? For Exempt positions, all applications will be reviewed at the same time. For posted OPSEU positions, applications from current OPSEU members will be reviewed prior to any external applications in accordance with the collective agreement. Where can I find additional information on the Exempt & OPSEU Recruitment process? Please refer to the Recruiting – Exempt & OPSEU Policy and OPSEU Collective Agreement , for further information. Action Menu 50/50 Employee Raffle Draw Anonymous HR Feedback Submission Heart of Trent Awards Non-Academic Positions Non-Academic Positions Important Information Before Applying Frequently Asked Questions Full-Time Faculty Positions (TUFA) Part-Time Faculty Positions (CUPE) Students & Alumni Student Academic Support Positions Related Links VIP - For Employees & Managers Health and Safety Human Rights, Equity & Accessibility Heart of Trent Event Trent University respectfully acknowledges it is located on the treaty and traditional territory of the Mississauga Anishnaabeg. We offer our gratitude to First Peoples for their care for, and teachings about, our earth and our relations. May we honour those teachings. The Campaign For Momentous Action Research Leadership Debate Performance Connection Discovery Ideas Places Stewardship Support Possiblity Peterborough 1600 West Bank Drive Peterborough, ON Canada, K9L 0G2 Toll Free: 1-855-MY-TRENT Find Us Durham Greater Toronto Area 55 Thornton Road South Oshawa, ON Canada, L1J 5Y1 Phone: 905-435-5100 Find Us Social Media Directory Contact Directions Site Map Accessibility Privacy @ Copyright 2026 Trent University This Site Uses Cookies To Enhance Your User Experience View Trent's privacy policy for more information. Accept"
    },
    "https://www.trentu.ca/humanresources/employment-opportunities/part-time-faculty-positions": {
